          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Richard A. Cordray, the petition by former Secretary of State Warren Christopher and others alleges denial of access to the courts by government officials."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Chief Justice Rehnquist",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3adc3796d5fbe028c595d0872ba8370ad2f608cf7edd039b4f9eb2f22a760638",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3adc3796d5fb-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Chief Justice Rehnquist, the justices raised questions about the right of access, referencing the Bell v. Milwaukee case and the Bivens doctrine."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3adc3796d5fbe028c595d0872ba8370ad2f608cf7edd039b4f9eb2f22a760638",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3adc3796d5fb-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 20,
              "start": 20
            }
          },
          {
            "document_hash": "3adc3796d5fbe028c595d0872ba8370ad2f608cf7edd039b4f9eb2f22a760638",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3adc3796d5fb-0001-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 24,
              "start": 24
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice, the Court also inquired whether statements were made with the intent to prevent a lawsuit, highlighting concerns about potential misuse of governmental information."
      }
    ],
